// Pseudocode — one thread block computes a M_TILE x N_TILE tile of C
// per iteration of the K-loop, it stages A[m0:m0+M_TILE, k:k+K_TILE]
// and B[k:k+K_TILE, n0:n0+N_TILE] into shared memory, then multiplies.
// Flops per K_TILE step:   2 * M_TILE * N_TILE * K_TILE
// Bytes read per K_TILE step (from HBM): (M_TILE + N_TILE) * K_TILE * sizeof(elt)
// Arithmetic intensity (per element type of A/B) ≈
//     (2 * M_TILE * N_TILE) / ((M_TILE + N_TILE) * sizeof(elt))
